<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/4th-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Siege</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alexander's siege of Tyre</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">332 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wars-of-alexander-the-great">Wars of Alexander the Great</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alexander's siege of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tyre">Tyre</a> was the siege of the Phoenician island city of Tyre by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-the-great">Alexander the Great</a> in 332 BCE. To reach the city, his engineers built a causeway from the mainland, and Tyre fell after about seven months. The siege showed Macedonian engineering skill and ended the independence of the mother city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a>, a connection noted in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punic-empire">Punic Empire</a>'s profile.</p></div>
